  "final_answer": "## Answer\n\n**Yes, apple.com currently advertises trade-in offers that apply to the latest iPhone model.**\n\n### Latest iPhone Models\nAccording to apple.com/iphone, the newest iPhone models (both marked \"New\") are:\n- **iPhone Duo** (featured first in the lineup, starting at $1,999 — described as \"The thinnest iPhone we've ever made\")\n- **iPhone 18 Pro** (starting at $1,199)\n\n### Trade-In Offers\nApple's Trade In program (apple.com/shop/trade-in) offers trade-in credit that can be **applied toward a qualifying new device purchase**, including the latest iPhones. Key points:\n\n- **Top iPhone trade-in values** (credit toward new iPhone Duo / iPhone 18 Pro):\n  - iPhone 17 Pro Max: Up to **$885**\n  - iPhone 17 Pro: Up to **$785**\n  - iPhone Air: Up to **$585**\n  - iPhone 17: Up to **$585**\n  - iPhone 16 Pro Max: Up to **$610**\n  - iPhone 16 Pro: Up to **$510**\n  - iPhone 16 Plus / iPhone 16: Up to **$430**\n  - And additional values going back to older models (iPhone 8 Plus: Up to $35, iPhone SE 2nd gen: Up to $40, etc.)\n\n- **Important note**: The newest models (iPhone Duo and iPhone 18 Pro) are not listed as devices with trade-in *values* — because they're the newest. However, the program explicitly states: *\"Trade-in value may be applied toward qualifying new device purchase, or added to an Apple Gift Card.\"* So customers can trade in any older eligible iPhone and use the credit to reduce the cost of the new iPhone Duo or iPhone 18 Pro.\n\n- **Eligibility requires** being at least the age of majority, with trade-in values varying based on condition, year, and configuration.",
